# Score B: notes copied from the English Wikisource page at its URL, under CC BY-SA 4.0; the page is the attribution. Retrieved 2026-11-07, used only to compare, never served.
# Verse 1 only. The tune is the one now sung ("Merrily We Roll Along"), traditional; it is not Lowell Mason's 1830s setting.
# Wikipedia attributes the same tune (chorus of "Goodnight, Ladies", 1867) to E. P. Christy (1815-1862); filed as traditional.
